{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "README": [
    "Entity seed list for bulk and block deals (docs/specs/04 section 5.3). Human-editable; the build reads it on every run.",
    "Matching: a client name is cleaned (upper case, '&' becomes AND, every run of non-letters or digits becomes one space, LIMITED becomes LTD, PRIVATE becomes PVT). A cleaned name matches an entity when one of its patterns appears in it as whole words. The first matching entity in this file wins, so list specific names before general ones.",
    "Unmatched names become their own entity: id = the cleaned name in lower case with spaces replaced by hyphens; the type is inferred (entityTypeInferred = true).",
    "Type inference, first rule that matches wins: an ODI account (name ends in ODI, e.g. '- ODI') -> FPI (likely); MUTUAL FUND or a trailing MF -> MF; INSURANCE or ASSURANCE -> Insurance; PENSION or PROVIDENT -> Pension; BANK -> Bank; PTE, PLC, LLC, FUND, SICAV, MAURITIUS or SINGAPORE -> FPI (likely); TRADING, SECURITIES, BROKING, CAPITAL MARKETS or LLP -> Trader/Prop (likely); otherwise Other.",
    "Category: FPI and FPI (likely) -> FII; MF, Insurance, Pension, Bank and AIF -> DII; everything else -> Other. An entity's own 'category' field overrides the derived value. The ODI rule is checked first, so an ODI account stays FII even when its name also contains BANK (see DEVIATIONS #76).",
    "Seeds: the largest names by deal value in the stored deals (2025-11-03 to 2026-11-13), grouped by firm. Foreign pension funds, sovereign funds and US trusts are set to FII explicitly, because the name rules would call them DII. Review and edit freely; the build and the tests read this file.",
    "Added after the coverage check (DEVIATIONS #76): the top 50 FII and top 50 DII names by value must each be a seed (tested). Integrated Insurance Broking Services is typed Other because it is a broker, not an insurer, so the name rule (INSURANCE -> DII) is overridden.",
    "Also set to FII by name (DEVIATIONS #76): the Hong Kong MPF unit trust (Manulife Provident Funds) and the Government Pension Fund Global account, which is Norway's sovereign fund.",
    "Factory Mutual Insurance (a US insurer) is typed Insurance by the name rule and listed here so it is covered; an overseas insurer may be FPI rather than DII, so review it."
  ],
